          The best protein powder for recovery is a fast-digesting whey isolate or hydrolysate that gives you 20 to 40 g of protein and about 2 to 3 g of leucine in one serving, taken within a few hours of training, on top of a daily intake of roughly 1.6 g/kg. Dymatize ISO100 Hydrolyzed is our top pick for most people; Momentous Whey Isolate and Optimum Nutrition Gold Standard (in its certified flavors) are the tested alternatives at premium and budget prices. The honest part: the famous anabolic window is much wider than supplement marketing suggests, protein does little for soreness on its own, and the add-ins with the best evidence, creatine and to a lesser degree tart cherry, are things you can buy separately. Below are the dose numbers, what the timing studies actually found, the difference between whey, hydrolysate and EAAs, and eight picks with a comparison table.
        </p>

