          </p>

          <p>
            That makes the choice of powder fairly simple. Look for a fast-digesting milk protein, ideally isolate or hydrolysate, with 20 to 40 g of protein and around 2 to 3 g of leucine per serving, a short label, and independent certification if you compete. Pay extra for hydrolysate only if regular whey upsets your stomach or you train twice a day. Add casein before bed if you struggle to hit your daily target.
