                  Whey protein, particularly isolate or hydrolysate, is the best-studied option because it digests quickly and contains plenty of leucine. A 20 to 40 g serving after training covers the post-workout dose for most people. Casein before bed and a certified plant blend are good alternatives depending on timing and diet.
                </p>
