            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Are EAAs better than protein powder for recovery?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Not usually. About 10 g of EAAs can maximally stimulate muscle protein synthesis, but a 20 to 25 g serving of whey supplies the same EAAs plus other amino acids, often at a lower cost. EAAs are useful mainly during training or for people who cannot tolerate a full shake.
                </p>
